      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You cannot replicate the sterile surgical environment a doctor provides, and even a tiny nick can introduce bacteria deep into your tissue, potentially turning a simple bump into a dangerous, spreading infection. Attempting to self-treat is risky because you may not fully remove the infected contents, leading to more severe pain, prolonged healing, or the formation of a adhesional scar. The cost of a proper medical visit is far less than the potential expense of treating a severe wound, so please prioritize your health and see a doctor or pharmacist for a safe and affordable solution.",
      "source": "target",
